    "intro_narrative": "The world ended decades ago, swallowed by nuclear fire and toxic ash. You are a Scrapper, surviving in the crumbling ruins of Sector 7. Disaster has struck your outpost: the central water filtration system has completely failed, and a deadly, suffocating rad-storm is approaching fast. Your settlement's only hope lies deep underground in an abandoned military bunker, rumored to house a legendary artifact known as the Creation Forge—an old-world matter synthesizer capable of fabricating any part from raw data blueprints. The bunker is a graveyard of dead systems, rusted terminals, and fragmented code left behind by the old military. To activate the Forge, you must restart the facility's decaying network, re-route power through forgotten nodes, and bypass heavy biometric security. The storm is howling on the surface, and time is running out. Reactivate the systems, synthesize the replacement part, and save your people before the ash claims you all.",
    "narrative_style": "post_apocalyptic"
  },
